Gul desktop includes React, React DOM, LiveKit JS, its generated
protocol code, and the JavaScript packages listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.
That directory includes license texts for the modules and font files actually
included in the main, preload, and renderer bundles, with exact versions.

IBM Plex Sans, IBM Plex Mono and Martian Mono use SIL Open Font License 1.1.
Fonts are bundled locally and are not fetched while the application runs.

Electron includes Chromium and Node.js. Their notices are distributed with
the Electron framework. Xray is a separate bundled executable; its license
and checked binary digest are distributed in the xray resource directory.

LiveKit server, TURN and the Gul session broker run separately and are not
embedded in this desktop application. The original Gul application license
is included as LICENSE.
